{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 170,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suppose you want to discover a particle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4230,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, you need to-"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5230,
    "dDurationMs": 13710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18940,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks for walking us through that point,\nJohn."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20690,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we're honest, we should say that the mathematical\nmodel for the Higgs was discovered in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25000,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1960s, but the particle itself wasn't dis-\nwasn't confirmed until 2012."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28789,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the Higgs boson ISN'T even the first\nnew particle to be... \"uncovered\" at the Large"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32679,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hadron Collider: the Xi-b particle, basically\na heavy version of the neutron, was actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37519,
    "dDurationMs": 1651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "found several months earlier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39170,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You probably didn't hear much about it because\nthe Xi-b is just a combination of quarks that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42760,
    "dDurationMs": 2590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we already know existÐ so it's not really\nthat exciting."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45350,
    "dDurationMs": 4449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, if you know about cheese and you know\nabout crackers, then the discovery of \"cheese"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49799,
    "dDurationMs": 3961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and crackers,\" as delightful as it is, isn't\nlikely to upend your universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53760,
    "dDurationMs": 3549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the Standard Model of particle physics\nalso predicts something beyond cheese and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57309,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crackers - that is, about one out of every\nbajillion collisions should produce a Higgs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61489,
    "dDurationMs": 3611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "boson, which then decays into everyday stuff\nlike electrons and photons, which are the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65100,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same crumbs we catch in the detector all the\ntime."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67990,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This battle between the tiny chance for a\ncollision to have produced a Higgs-like particle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71380,
    "dDurationMs": 3809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "versus all the trizillion other collisions\nthat produce similar crumbs is part of why"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75189,
    "dDurationMs": 2911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need a big machine like the Large Hadron\nCollider at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78100,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There were earlier accelerators that had enough\nenergy to create Higgs bosons in principle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81670,
    "dDurationMs": 3549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- but they couldn't actually do enough collisions\nto be confident they were actually seeing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85219,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Higgs boson and not just an assortment of\ncrumbs that looks by chance like it's from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88829,
    "dDurationMs": 1051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Higgs Boson."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89880,
    "dDurationMs": 2879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's kind of like trying to find out if a\n20-sided die is rigged."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92759,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe you suspect it's twice as likely to\nland on a three than on any of the other numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96689,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how can you check?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97689,
    "dDurationMs": 3481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, that sounds easy enough - just roll\nthe die a few times and if you see extra threes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101170,
    "dDurationMs": 1150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's rigged, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102320,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not so fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103320,
    "dDurationMs": 3839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if you roll the die ten times,\nthere's a pretty good chance that you won't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107159,
    "dDurationMs": 1590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get any threes at all!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108749,
    "dDurationMs": 3101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because even though rolling a three\nis twice as likely as all the other numbers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111850,
    "dDurationMs": 2559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are still a lot of other numbers you\ncould roll."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114409,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So random chance and big numbers can be surprisingly\ndeceptive - even if you roll the die a hundred"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118859,
    "dDurationMs": 5751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times and DO get an excess of threes, there's\nstill a one in fifty chance that the die IS"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124610,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fair and you just got this number by accident."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125610,
    "dDurationMs": 2109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How much are you willing to bet that you actually\nhave evidence for a new particle if there's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127719,
    "dDurationMs": 3692,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a one in fifty chance your results are simply\na random fluctuation and the particle doesn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131411,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually exist?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132411,
    "dDurationMs": 3869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What if a Nobel Prize is on the line - how\nsure do you want to be?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136280,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One in a thousand?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137280,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One in ten thousand?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138280,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually, physicists are even more stringent\nthey won't say they've \"discovered\" a particle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141090,
    "dDurationMs": 2009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unless the odds that they might get the same\nresults even if the particle DOESN'T exist"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143099,
    "dDurationMs": 2871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are less than one in a million…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145970,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you want to convince a particle physicist\nthat you've discovered an unfair die, you'll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150340,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "need to roll over five hundred and fifty times\nto satisfy them!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153400,
    "dDurationMs": 3259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's just to check if a twenty-sided\ndie is rigged – there are far more than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156659,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "twenty possible outcomes of a high-energy\nparticle collision, so in order to be confident"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160159,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about announcing evidence for a new particle\nat the LHC, you need around 600 million collisions…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165069,
    "dDurationMs": 1971,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every second… for two years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167040,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only then can you uncork the wine to go with\nyour cheese and crackers, and claim a successful"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171260,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "discov– I mean, successful scientific fact-checking."
    } ]
  } ]
}
